  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Commissioner Lindsay S. See described growing electricity demand from AI, manufacturing, and other strategic sectors as a national opportunity rather than a crisis if met. She said that, when done right, co-location can be consumer-forward and help meet a national imperative of speed to power and winning the AI race. She identified encouraging as much flexibility as responsibly possible for novel approaches as one of her guideposts. She also said that when deployed well, such strategies can be consumer-forward and help meet the same national imperative.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s3",
    "s2",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
